      "comment": "MILLIONAIRE LOVER (3) capped off some strong form to record his first win when scoring out of her grade in class 2 company here nearly 4 weeks ago. This is no harder, and with the same weight to carry, he can now go right on with the job. VATICAN ROSE (4) was an overdue maiden winner here 3 weeks ago, and she can take up the pace again after drawing in the pole position. She is down 2kg with the rise in class, and she has the scope to take the next step immediately. VORONYA (1) is a very progressive local gelding who ended his last prep as an easy class 2 winner here at the start of this season. His recent spell would have done him the world of good, and the only query would be having to shoulder 61kg. Hard to beat again. YULE POINT (2) resumed with a brave effort for second as the favourite over 1100m. The extra 100m is ideal, and he can go one better in a very handy contest. YOU'RESOGOLDEN (5) will be peaking third up, and her first local win is not far away.",
